[{:seon.task/name "landed-tells-the-sessions-it-unblocks"
  :seon.task/plan "Plan Stage 1.8 (root, 2026-11-14): when a landing completes what a task needed, the sessions waiting on it are told, so no session polls and none messages another about it. Who waits: the live agents (a model agent or a Claude session's outside agent) of the tasks whose :seon.task/needs name a task that just merged. One pure function, my.root/landed-messages [db ids]: for each id merged on db, each such agent's key and a body naming what landed (its id and main's t) and the form that takes it, (my.branch/merge-main!); an agent of a task that needs nothing landed is told nothing; an ended agent is told nothing. Two callers, one way to send: the reconciler where a task merges (seon.reconcile's :octopus-merged) sends each as it sends a stage boundary, a :message request from :root, which the writer's answer wakes (seon.system's :message op); and, until a session's change merges through seon_done (seon.server/a-sessions-file-edit-merges-through-done), bin/land after LANDED calls my.root/landed! with its Completes: ids (seon.system/message! passes :from through). Estimate: one seek of :seon.task/needs reversed per landed id, one of each needing task's agents; a message write each."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.reconcile-test/a-merge-tells-the-agents-whose-tasks-need-it}}]
